// ADR-009 C2 slice 5 — a replace-body EDIT installs and runs natively in both
// tiers. The comptime `post` handler replaces `answer`'s body; the POST-edit
// body (42) is what executes, while the pre-edit body (7) is preserved as the
// hygienic `ctx.original` shadow. Printing 42 — not 7 — proves the edited body
// runs. The runtime program is a plain int function + its dead shadow + a call;
// no async, trait/impl, closure, or top-level comptime, so JIT == VM natively
// (zero [jit-fallback]).
annotation edit_answer() on function {
  comptime post(target, ctx) {
    replace body { return 42 }
  }
}

@edit_answer()
fn answer() -> int { 7 }

print(answer())
